I've recorded the input and sampling plan for H1388 and moved it to PLAN_REVIEW. I haven't written the plan brief or opened the checkpoint yet; that is the next step.

**What I found:** a full set of predictions from the earlier CASP17 run is already on disk under `/gpfs/deepfold/casp/casp17/targets/H1388/results`. It covers both copy numbers (one peptide on one 14-3-3, and the 14-3-3 dimer with two peptides) and three input variants: the AF3 MSA, the same MSA with phosphoserine at LARP1 S548, and the mmseqs2 MSA.
- **AF3:** 25 seeds × 5 samples per combination.
- **BT2 and OF3:** both copy numbers, but only without the phosphoserine.
- **PT2:** no model files in any combination, even though the logs end with "done".

I recorded this as evidence (`existing_pool`).

**Decisions:**
- **D3, MSA:** keep the existing 14-3-3 alignments, which are already deep (uniref90 6,536 sequences, uniprot 16,347). The 11-residue LARP1 peptide runs as a single sequence, since a peptide that short has no useful homologs.
- **D4, templates:** keep AF3's default template search. 91 of its 1,578 hits are 14-3-3 gamma itself, including structures with a peptide bound. If the peptide's position in the groove varies between models at the results review, a custom template from 6A5S or 2B05 is the fallback.
- **D5, ligands:** none. The only chemistry is the phosphoserine variant already decided in D1.
- **D6, sampling:** no new GPU runs now; reuse the roughly 1,400 existing models. Selection will check that peptide serine 7 sits in the 14-3-3 phosphate pocket (residues 49, 56, 131, 132). I set aside up to 40 of the 400 GPU-hours to rerun PT2, and to run OF3/BT2 with the phosphoserine if it puts the peptide in a different place than the unmodified input.

**Next step:** build the slide report, write the plan brief and open `lantern consult H1388 --kind plan`. The questions for the person will be whether to reuse the pool, whether to rerun PT2 and run the other predictors with the phosphoserine, and whether to use the custom template.

